# Multilingual Processing Layer Implementation

The goal is to introduce a multilingual layer that supports English, Hindi, and Marathi without modifying the core logic of the existing ML classifier (Chain 1) or breaking the Evidence Verification pipeline (Chain 2).

## Proposed Changes

### Dependencies
- Add `langdetect` to `requirements.txt` for fast, local language identification.
- Add `deep-translator` to `requirements.txt` as a deterministic translation service (Google Translate API) to translate Hindi and Marathi into English for Chain 1, avoiding unnecessary Gemini translation calls.

### Database (`backend/app/database/history_models.py`)
- **[MODIFY]** `PredictionHistory` model to include:
  - `original_text` (Text)
  - `detected_language` (String)
  - `translated_text` (Text)
  - `translation_status` (String)
  - `user_output_language` (String)
- **Note**: A small SQLite migration script will be executed to run `ALTER TABLE prediction_history ADD COLUMN ...` to safely accommodate the new metadata without breaking existing records.

### Backend Services
#### [NEW] `backend/app/services/multilingual_analysis_service.py`
- Implements `LanguageDetectionService` using `langdetect` with a confidence threshold.
- Implements `TranslationService` using `deep-translator` (GoogleTranslator) to translate Marathi and Hindi into English.
- Acts as an adapter that coordinates the pipeline: extracts/combines text -> detects language -> translates (if needed) -> invokes the existing `PredictionService.predict(english_text)` -> returns combined results.

#### [MODIFY] `backend/app/services/gemini_evidence_service.py`
- Update `verify_evidence` to accept `original_text`, `detected_language`, `translated_text`, `ml_result`, and `user_output_language`.
- Enhance the `system_instruction` to include the specific instructions provided in the requirements, ensuring Gemini searches in the original language first, and outputs the final explanation in the `user_output_language`.

#### [MODIFY] API Routes (`predict.py`, `url.py`, `image.py`, `pdf.py`)
- Update all these endpoints to use `MultilingualAnalysisService.process_and_predict` instead of directly calling `PredictionService.predict`.
- This ensures all inputs (PDF, Voice, QR, URL, Raw Text, Image) automatically benefit from the multilingual layer.

#### [MODIFY] Schemas (`backend/app/schemas/prediction.py`, `evidence.py`, `history.py`)
- Update `PredictionResponse` to return the new multilingual fields.
- Update `EvidenceRequest` to receive the multilingual context and Chain 1 results.
- Update `HistoryCreate` and `HistoryResponse` to persist the new multilingual fields.

### Frontend Integration
#### [MODIFY] `frontend/src/pages/Analyze.jsx`
- Update `handleResult` to pass the new fields from `mlResponse` (`detected_language`, `translated_text`, `prediction`, etc.) into `analyzeEvidence`.
- **Note on UI Language Selector**: The instructions mention an existing language selection UI. If it exists in the codebase (e.g., local storage preference), I will read from it. If it doesn't currently exist in the frontend UI, I will add a minimal `user_output_language` state (defaulting to English) to ensure the full pipeline can be tested, as instructed by "Do not rebuild the language-selection UI. Connect it."

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- No formal unit tests are currently present, but manual testing of the API endpoints will be conducted using `curl` or Postman.

### Manual Verification
- Test all input sources (Raw Text, URL, PDF, Image, Voice) with English, Hindi, and Marathi inputs using the frontend UI.
- Verify that Chain 1 successfully produces a prediction for Marathi/Hindi text by acting on the English translation.
- Verify that the Gemini backend log shows it received the original Marathi/Hindi text and the Chain 1 ML result.
- Verify the final Gemini response is in the requested `user_output_language`.

